recision deltas \u0394PPL = PPL(quant) \u2212 PPL(FP16) and \u0394acc = acc(quant) \u2212 acc(FP16) with tolerance bands from the paper (approximately \u0394PPL within \u00b10.1\u20130.3 and \u0394acc within \u00b11\u20132 pts for 4-bit). Verdicts: \"pure speed boost\" if C1 shows speedup within CI AND \u0394 stays inside bands while C2 (RTN) shows \u0394 clearly outside bands; \"speed/accuracy tradeoff\" if C1's \u0394 is material; otherwise quantify the magnitude. Report per phase (prefill vs decode) so the answer states, e.g., decode gains X\u00d7 but prefill only Y\u00d7.\nSensitivity sub-experiment (budget permitting, on 7B only): calibration set RedPajama(canonical 512\u00d72048) vs C4, and group size 128 vs 64, to bound calibration dependence.\n\n(e) FEASIBILITY & RISKS\nEstimated budget (1\u00d7 H100): calibration ~0.5\u20131.5 h per model (512\u00d72048 tokens); quantization minutes per model; inference grid ~ (3 sizes\u00d74 configs\u00d74 lengths\u00d73 batches\u00d75 repeats) \u2014 roughly 1\u20132 days per model at L2, dominated by 70B B\u22658; Tier A (7B+13B) fits comfortably within ~2\u20133 GPU-days; Tier B (70B) adds ~1\u20132 GPU-days. These are design estimates to size the repetition/trim tradeoff.\nSetup steps on target: install pinned torch/transformers/datasets/lm-eval-harness and vLLM (QuaRot fork); clone spcl-graph/QuaRot at fixed commit; build CUDA kernels via its Dockerfile; download gated LLaMa-2 checkpoints; quantize once per config and save checkpoints; run L1 and L2 benches; run quality evals with the same checkpoint.\nRisks & mitigations:\n  R1 Gated weights unavailable \u2192 blocker for the exact task; mitigation = pre-request HF access, mirror fallback; if unresolvable, the design stands but LLaMa-2 must be swapped (flag clearly, changes the answer).\n  R2 Kernel build failure (CUDA/PyTorch mismatch) \u2192 pin repo CI versions; use repo's Docker image; do NOT fall back to FP16 fallback kernels (would invalidate W4A4).\n  R3 QuaRot precision-mapping config ambiguity (INT4 weights vs FP8 activations/KV) \u2192 read and freeze the mapping from the pinned commit's config file and document it verbatim; all results referenced to that mapping.\n  R4 Clock control unavailable \u2192 raise n, interleave, and report observed clock spread.\n  R5 vLLM-fork divergence \u2192 rely on L2 phase-pure microbench as primary where L1/L2 disagree, and document both.\nArtifacts: quantized checkpoints, raw timing logs + per-run values, aggregated tables, bootstrap CIs, and a results summary answering the question with a per-model speed/accuracy verdict and explicit phase split. Runbook scripts + requirements.lock committed for reproducibility.\n\nSTATEMENT: This is a design specification only; no experiment was executed, and no results are claimed.", "evidence": "Inspected /workspace (only task.json + track.md stub), full filesystem search for quarot/vllm/lm_eval/llama (none), /opt /root /tmp empty, no wheels/pip cache, net disabled (curl to pypi timed out), no GPU (nvidia-smi fails), 224 CPUs/2TB RAM, git 2.53 present, torch/transformers/datasets/accelerate/numpy all MISSING \u2014 confirming a pure design task. Method details (online Hadamard rotation, KQ rotation for 4-bit KV, W4A4, RedPajama 512x2048 calibration, lm-eval accuracy suite) grounded in QuaRot ICLR 2025 paper and the official spcl-graph/QuaRot repo (benchmark_latency/throughput paths, fused-CUDA-kernel build, vLLM fork). Per-phase reasoning (compute-bound prefill vs memory-bound decode) and paired-test/ratio-of-means aggregation follow standard benchmarking practice.", "assumptions": ["'Performance' means both speed (latency/throughput) and quality (PPL/accuracy); both measured", "Target hardware is 1x H100-80GB or A100-80GB with unstated runtime budget", "LLaMa-2 7B/13B/70B weights obtainable via gated HF access", "Official QuaRot repo pinned at a fixed commit; CUDA kernels build in its Docker image", "Paper-default calibration (RedPajama 512x2048) with a 7B-only C4/group-size sensitivity check", "Both vLLM application-level and kernel-level measurements in scope; kernel-level is primary where they disagree", "Tier A (7B+13B) is the guaranteed scope; 70B is contingent on VRAM/budget"], "uncertainties": ["Actual GPU VRAM and total compute budget (drives 70B inclusion and n/repetition trim)", "LLaMa-2 gated-weight availability (hard blocker if denied)", "Exact internal precision mapping (INT4 vs FP8 for activations/KV) must be frozen from the pinned commit config", "Ability to pin GPU clocks; observed clock variance handled as noise via interleaving", "vLLM-fork behavior vs phase-pure kernel microbenchmark; disagreement resolved in favor of L2 and documented", "Real runtime may differ from 1-2 GPU-days per model estimate (estimation only)"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-e438ab8779d14d14ac384ad8598b34ea", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Submit full QuaRot W4A4 prefill/decode experiment design", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
